                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fbeb2316-f29c-38ee-b961-d43929033261",
                                        "entry_id": "4e49632a-3267-35c7-8258-4a30b76d9006",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A patch of colour around an animal's upper breast and throat."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c94f3568-8525-437c-868c-a92094c50146",
                                                "sense_id": "fbeb2316-f29c-38ee-b961-d43929033261",
                                                "text": "In summer the whole throat and breast are black, but in winter plumage the throat is white bounded by a horseshoe-shaped black bib."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f8025f83-312a-4e22-8b53-646aa44b62f6",
                                                "sense_id": "fbeb2316-f29c-38ee-b961-d43929033261",
                                                "text": "He don't look anything like the captain. This here cat has got a nice thick black coat of fur with a nice white bib and white feet."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e0ada725-787f-3eba-96d1-4691bee09705",
                                        "entry_id": "4e49632a-3267-35c7-8258-4a30b76d9006",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A north Atlantic fish (Trisopterus luscus), allied to the cod."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4b0b4bb4-a3ac-35d9-94ba-25974e965f75",
                                        "entry_id": "4e49632a-3267-35c7-8258-4a30b76d9006",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A bibb (bibcock)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "bib",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7e6e5635-fc33-3e36-bad7-562d6014e936",
                                        "entry_id": "7bef1040-d86a-38bd-b253-219684bba1b2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To dress (somebody) in a bib."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fc33ad6a-d78f-4a08-8cfe-fdd8053ffe08",
                                                "sense_id": "7e6e5635-fc33-3e36-bad7-562d6014e936",
                                                "text": "Wise women use them, but new fathers seldom seem to understand that one minute bibbing baby saves who knows how long swabbing, finding clean clothes, changing, and coddling later — not to mention laundry time."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1d1ab247-931f-4c5e-b0cd-d00bc13fdadc",
                                                "sense_id": "7e6e5635-fc33-3e36-bad7-562d6014e936",
                                                "text": "Mel got Daniel into his chair and bibbed him up."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5a5afd2c-38a5-31a3-b771-8c5b6906c4ff",
                                        "entry_id": "7bef1040-d86a-38bd-b253-219684bba1b2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To drink heartily; to tipple."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f7381ed9-2e57-4970-897d-59e694b561e5",
                                                "sense_id": "5a5afd2c-38a5-31a3-b771-8c5b6906c4ff",
                                                "text": "Iff I were a fleſhly felowe, and a preacher of lyes and tolde them that they might ſyt bebbinge and bollynge, and be droncken: O that were a prophet for this people."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "42889fac-4979-46f6-900f-43f074937837",
                                                "sense_id": "5a5afd2c-38a5-31a3-b771-8c5b6906c4ff",
                                                "text": "they gave him drink as often as he cry'd; so that he was constantly bibbing"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
